 34AR    COULOMB EXCITATION            2023DR01                  ENSDF    202609
 34AR  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34AR c  2023Dr01: An intermediate Coulomb excitation experiment was performed  
 34AR2c  to measure the 0+ |) 2+ B(E2) value of {+36,38}Ca. {+34}Ar beam was a  
 34AR3c  contaminant produced from the fragmentation of a 140 MeV/nucleon       
 34AR4c  {+40}Ca primary beam delivered by the Coupled Cyclotron Facility at the
 34AR5c  National Superconducting Cyclotron Laboratory (NSCL) impinging upon an 
 34AR6c  800-mg/cm{+2}-thick {+9}Be production target and separated using a     
 34AR7c  300-mg/cm{+2} Al wedge degrader in the A1900 fragment separator.       
 34AR8c  Secondary beam was scattered off a 257-mg/cm{+2}-thick Au foil located 
 34AR9c  at the target position of the S800 spectrograph. The deexciting |g rays
 34ARAc  were detected using GRETINA surrounding the S800 spectrograph. The     
 34ARBc  GRETINA comprised a total of 48 HPGe crystals; 32 of them at 90|' and  
 34ARCc  16 of them at 58|' with respect to the beam direction. The inelastic   
 34ARDc  excitations of the projectile and target nuclei were quantified with   
 34AREc  the detection of prompt |g rays in GRETINA. The scattered projectiles  
 34ARFc  were identified using S800 focal plane detection system together with  
 34ARGc  tof measurement. Measured: E|g, tof, cross section and B(E2).          
 34ARHc  Comparison with the shell model calculations.                          
